From b40f340b16bc1d2ff1593eccd34a7197a6ca67bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:26:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Software rendering for the GUI and 4096-byte boot filesystem,
 both in the rom workflow

Black screen: with the renderer unpinned, phoc/wlroots (and KWin) try GLES2
through Panfrost first and the screen stays black with the session running.
The device package now pins software rendering in a separate drop-in per UI
(phosh: WLR_RENDERER=pixman, LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1, GSK_RENDERER=cairo;
plasma-mobile: KWIN_COMPOSE=Q, QT_QUICK_BACKEND=software,
LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1) so deleting one file brings the GPU path back, and
installs x6525-display-report to collect what is needed to diagnose a black
screen. pkgrel 21.

UFS units: a UFS LUN has 4096-byte blocks and U-Boot cannot read the 1024-byte
block boot filesystem pmbootstrap makes ("Read outside partition ..."). The rom
job rebuilds pmos-boot-fs.img with 4096-byte blocks (tools/reblock-boot-fs.sh,
label and UUID kept, contents compared) and a new step fails the build if
either image has smaller blocks or the software-render drop-in is missing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XFxAXRoPDmghVRawP2Mf9h
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml                      |  47 ++++++++
 BRING_UP_CHECKLIST.md                         |  24 +++-
 FIRST_BOOT.md                                 |   8 ++
 .../testing/device-infinix-x6525/APKBUILD     | 113 +++++++++++++++--
 tools/audit-features.sh                       |   7 +-
 tools/reblock-boot-fs.sh                      | 114 ++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 298 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tools/reblock-boot-fs.sh

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index cb1f190..ad73bcb 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -400,11 +400,58 @@ jobs:
           bc=$((bc + 8 * 1048576 / bs))
           resize2fs "$B" "$bc"
           truncate -s $((bs * bc)) "$B"
+          # pmbootstrap makes this small filesystem with 1024-byte blocks. A UFS unit's
+          # LUN has 4096-byte blocks, and U-Boot (and Linux) cannot read a filesystem
+          # whose blocks are smaller than the device's: U-Boot prints "Read outside
+          # partition 9223372036854775808" on the UFS `cache` partition. 4096-byte
+          # blocks read fine on eMMC too, so rebuild it that way (label and UUID kept).
+          sh tools/reblock-boot-fs.sh "$B" 4096
           e2fsck -fn "$B"
           ls -l "$B"
           python3 -I tools/check-boot-fs.py /tmp/rom-out/pmos-boot-fs.img || echo "::warning::boot fs check failed"
           ls -la /tmp/rom-out/
 
+      - name: Check the images for the two known first-boot problems
+        env:
+          UI: ${{ inputs.ui || 'phosh' }}
+        run: |
+          B=/tmp/rom-out/pmos-boot-fs.img
+          R=/tmp/rom-out/pmos-root-fs.img
+          fail=0
+          bsz() { dumpe2fs -h "$1" 2>/dev/null | awk '/^Block size:/{print $3}'; }
+          # 1. both filesystems must be readable on a UFS unit (4096-byte blocks)
+          for f in "$B" "$R"; do
+            bs=$(bsz "$f")
+            if [ "${bs:-0}" -ge 4096 ]; then
+              echo "ok: $(basename "$f") has $bs-byte blocks"
+            else
+              echo "::error::$(basename "$f") has ${bs:-unknown}-byte blocks; a UFS unit (4096-byte blocks) cannot read it"
+              fail=1
+            fi
+          done
+          # 2. the session must be pinned to software rendering. Hardware GLES through
+          #    Panfrost is what leaves the screen black on this board, so the drop-in
+          #    that selects pixman (phoc) / QPainter (KWin) has to be in the image.
+          want() { # file pattern
+            if debugfs -R "cat $1" "$R" 2>/dev/null | grep -q "$2"; then
+              echo "ok: $1 sets $2"
+            else
+              echo "::error::$1 is missing or does not set $2"
+              fail=1
+            fi
+          }
+          case "$UI" in
+            phosh)
+              want /etc/systemd/system/greetd.service.d/20-x6525-software-render.conf '^Environment=WLR_RENDERER=pixman'
+              want /etc/systemd/system/greetd.service.d/20-x6525-software-render.conf '^Environment=LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1' ;;
+            plasma-mobile)
+              want /etc/systemd/system/plasma-mobile.service.d/20-x6525-software-render.conf '^Environment=KWIN_COMPOSE=Q'
+              want /etc/systemd/system/plasma-mobile.service.d/20-x6525-software-render.conf '^Environment=LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1' ;;
+          esac
+          debugfs -R "stat /usr/bin/x6525-display-report" "$R" 2>/dev/null | grep -q . ||
+            { echo "::error::/usr/bin/x6525-display-report is not in the image"; fail=1; }
+          [ "$fail" = 0 ] || exit 1
+
       - name: Upload it
         uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
         with:
